{"v":15,"id":"e03","kid":"emma","title":"Why Do Leaves Change Color?","zh":"树叶为什么会变色？","level":"B1","genre":"科学","src":"facts","sum":"叶绿素让树叶呈绿色；秋天树停止制造叶绿素，原本藏着的黄色、橙色就显露出来，有的树还会产生新的红色物质。最后树叶脱落，帮助树过冬。","words":264,"paras":[{"t":"In many parts of the world, autumn is a colorful season. Leaves that were green all summer turn yellow, orange and red. Then they fall to the ground. Why does this happen?","w":[[0,2,"in",-1],[3,7,"many",-1],[8,13,"parts",-1],[14,16,"of",-1],[17,20,"the",-1],[21,26,"world",-1],[28,34,"autumn",-1],[35,37,"is",-1],[38,39,"a",-1],[40,48,"colorful",-1],[49,55,"season",-1],[57,63,"leaves",-1],[64,68,"that",-1],[69,73,"were",-1],[74,79,"green",-1],[80,83,"all",-1],[84,90,"summer",-1],[91,95,"turn",-1],[96,102,"yellow",-1],[104,110,"orange",-1],[111,114,"and",-1],[115,118,"red",-1],[120,124,"then",-1],[125,129,"they",-1],[130,134,"fall",-1],[135,137,"to",-1],[138,141,"the",-1],[142,148,"ground",-1],[150,153,"why",-1],[154,158,"does",-1],[159,163,"this",-1],[164,170,"happen",-1]]},{"t":"The answer starts with a green substance called chlorophyll. Leaves use chlorophyll to make food for the tree. With the help of sunlight, chlorophyll turns water and carbon dioxide, a gas in the air, into sugar. Because there is so much chlorophyll in leaves in spring and summer, its green color covers up all the other colors.","w":[[0,3,"the",-1],[4,10,"answer",-1],[11,17,"starts",-1],[18,22,"with",-1],[23,24,"a",-1],[25,30,"green",-1],[31,40,"substance",-1],[41,47,"called",-1],[48,59,"chlorophyll",-1],[61,67,"leaves",-1],[68,71,"use",-1],[72,83,"chlorophyll",-1],[84,86,"to",-1],[87,91,"make",-1],[92,96,"food",-1],[97,100,"for",-1],[101,104,"the",-1],[105,109,"tree",-1],[111,115,"with",9],[116,119,"the",9],[120,124,"help",9],[125,127,"of",9],[128,136,"sunlight",-1],[138,149,"chlorophyll",-1],[150,155,"turns",-1],[156,161,"water",-1],[162,165,"and",-1],[166,172,"carbon",0],[173,180,"dioxide",0],[182,183,"a",-1],[184,187,"gas",-1],[188,190,"in",-1],[191,194,"the",-1],[195,198,"air",-1],[200,204,"into",-1],[205,210,"sugar",-1],[212,219,"because",-1],[220,225,"there",-1],[226,228,"is",-1],[229,231,"so",-1],[232,236,"much",-1],[237,248,"chlorophyll",-1],[249,251,"in",-1],[252,258,"leaves",-1],[259,261,"in",-1],[262,268,"spring",-1],[269,272,"and",-1],[273,279,"summer",-1],[281,284,"its",-1],[285,290,"green",-1],[291,296,"color",-1],[297,303,"covers",1],[304,306,"up",1],[307,310,"all",-1],[311,314,"the",-1],[315,320,"other",-1],[321,327,"colors",-1]]},{"t":"But leaves also contain yellow and orange substances. They are there all year, hidden under the green. Carrots get their orange color from one of these substances, too.","w":[[0,3,"but",-1],[4,10,"leaves",-1],[11,15,"also",-1],[16,23,"contain",-1],[24,30,"yellow",-1],[31,34,"and",-1],[35,41,"orange#2",-1],[42,52,"substances",-1],[54,58,"they",-1],[59,62,"are",-1],[63,68,"there",-1],[69,72,"all",2],[73,77,"year",2],[79,85,"hidden",-1],[86,91,"under",-1],[92,95,"the",-1],[96,101,"green",-1],[103,110,"carrots",-1],[111,114,"get",-1],[115,120,"their",-1],[121,127,"orange",-1],[128,133,"color",-1],[134,138,"from",-1],[139,142,"one",-1],[143,145,"of",-1],[146,151,"these",-1],[152,162,"substances",-1],[164,167,"too",-1]]},{"t":"When autumn comes, the days get shorter and the nights get cooler. In winter there is not enough sunlight or water for leaves to make much food, so trees get ready to rest. They stop making chlorophyll. As the green slowly disappears, the yellow and orange colors finally show.","w":[[0,4,"when",-1],[5,11,"autumn",-1],[12,17,"comes",-1],[19,22,"the",-1],[23,27,"days",-1],[28,31,"get",-1],[32,39,"shorter",-1],[40,43,"and",-1],[44,47,"the",-1],[48,54,"nights",-1],[55,58,"get",-1],[59,65,"cooler",-1],[67,69,"in",-1],[70,76,"winter",-1],[77,82,"there",-1],[83,85,"is",-1],[86,89,"not",-1],[90,96,"enough",-1],[97,105,"sunlight",-1],[106,108,"or",-1],[109,114,"water",-1],[115,118,"for",-1],[119,125,"leaves",-1],[126,128,"to",-1],[129,133,"make",-1],[134,138,"much",-1],[139,143,"food",-1],[145,147,"so",-1],[148,153,"trees",-1],[154,157,"get",3],[158,163,"ready",3],[164,166,"to",-1],[167,171,"rest",-1],[173,177,"they",-1],[178,182,"stop",-1],[183,189,"making",-1],[190,201,"chlorophyll",-1],[203,205,"as",-1],[206,209,"the",-1],[210,215,"green",-1],[216,222,"slowly",-1],[223,233,"disappears",-1],[235,238,"the",-1],[239,245,"yellow",-1],[246,249,"and",-1],[250,256,"orange",-1],[257,263,"colors",-1],[264,271,"finally",-1],[272,276,"show",-1]]},{"t":"What about red? Red is a little different. Some trees, like many maples, make new red substances in autumn. Sunny days and cool (but not freezing) nights help them produce bright red leaves. That is why some autumns are more colorful than others.","w":[[0,4,"what",4],[5,10,"about",4],[11,14,"red",-1],[16,19,"red#2",-1],[20,22,"is",-1],[23,24,"a",5],[25,31,"little",5],[32,41,"different",-1],[43,47,"some",-1],[48,53,"trees#2",-1],[55,59,"like",-1],[60,64,"many",-1],[65,71,"maples",-1],[73,77,"make",-1],[78,81,"new",-1],[82,85,"red",-1],[86,96,"substances",-1],[97,99,"in",-1],[100,106,"autumn",-1],[108,113,"sunny",-1],[114,118,"days",-1],[119,122,"and",-1],[123,127,"cool",-1],[129,132,"but",-1],[133,136,"not",-1],[137,145,"freezing",-1],[147,153,"nights",-1],[154,158,"help",-1],[159,163,"them",-1],[164,171,"produce",-1],[172,178,"bright",-1],[179,182,"red",-1],[183,189,"leaves",-1],[191,195,"that",-1],[196,198,"is",-1],[199,202,"why",-1],[203,207,"some",-1],[208,215,"autumns",-1],[216,219,"are",-1],[220,224,"more",-1],[225,233,"colorful",-1],[234,238,"than",-1],[239,245,"others",-1]]},{"t":"Finally, a thin layer of cells grows where each leaf joins its branch. This layer slowly cuts the leaf off from the tree, and the leaf falls. Dropping its leaves helps the tree save water during the cold, dry winter.","w":[[0,7,"finally",-1],[9,10,"a",-1],[11,15,"thin",-1],[16,21,"layer",-1],[22,24,"of",-1],[25,30,"cells",-1],[31,36,"grows",-1],[37,42,"where",-1],[43,47,"each",-1],[48,52,"leaf",-1],[53,58,"joins",-1],[59,62,"its",-1],[63,69,"branch",-1],[71,75,"this",-1],[76,81,"layer",-1],[82,88,"slowly",-1],[89,93,"cuts",6],[94,97,"the",6],[98,102,"leaf",6],[103,106,"off",6],[107,111,"from",-1],[112,115,"the",-1],[116,120,"tree",-1],[122,125,"and",-1],[126,129,"the",-1],[130,134,"leaf",-1],[135,140,"falls",-1],[142,150,"dropping",-1],[151,154,"its",-1],[155,161,"leaves",-1],[162,167,"helps",-1],[168,171,"the",-1],[172,176,"tree",-1],[177,181,"save",-1],[182,187,"water",-1],[188,194,"during",-1],[195,198,"the",-1],[199,203,"cold",-1],[205,208,"dry",-1],[209,215,"winter",-1]]},{"t":"Next time you see a red maple leaf, remember: you are watching science in action.","w":[[0,4,"next",7],[5,9,"time",7],[10,13,"you",-1],[14,17,"see",-1],[18,19,"a",-1],[20,23,"red",-1],[24,29,"maple",-1],[30,34,"leaf",-1],[36,44,"remember",-1],[46,49,"you",-1],[50,53,"are",-1],[54,62,"watching",-1],[63,70,"science",-1],[71,73,"in",8],[74,80,"action",8]]}],"gl":{"in":["in","/ɪn/","prep. 在……里；在（某时）","override"],"many":["many","/ˈmeni/","adj. 许多的","override"],"parts":["part","/pɑrts/","n. 部分","level"],"of":["of","/ʌv/","prep. ……的；属于","override"],"the":["the","/ðə/","art. 这个，那个（特指）","override"],"world":["world","/wɜrld/","n. 世界","level"],"autumn":["autumn","/ˈɔtəm/","秋天","level"],"is":["be","/ɪz/","v. 是","common"],"a":["a","/ə/","art. 一（个）","override"],"colorful":["colorful","/ˈkʌlərfəl/","adj. 色彩丰富的；五颜六色的","common"],"season":["season","/ˈsizən/","季节","level"],"leaves":["leaves","/livz/","叶子（leaf 的复数）","hand"],"that":["that","/ðæt/","pron. 那，那个","override"],"were":["were","/wɜr/","v. 是（are 的过去式）","common"],"green":["green","/ɡrin/","adj. 绿色的","level"],"all":["all","/ɔl/","det. 全部，所有","override"],"summer":["summer","/ˈsʌmər/","夏天","level"],"turn":["turn","/tɜrn/","v. 转动","override"],"yellow":["yellow","/ˈjeloʊ/","adj. 黄色的","level"],"orange":["orange","/ˈɔrəndʒ/","n. 橙子","override"],"and":["and","/ənd/","conj. 和","level"],"red":["red","/red/","adj. 红的，红色的","ecdict-pos"],"then":["then","/ðen/","adv. 那